{
  "$schema": "https://unpkg.com/knip@6/schema.json",

  // ⛔ EVERY IGNORE CARRIES A DISCRIMINATOR — a way to tell a knip BLIND SPOT from
  // a defect here. A bare ignore is how a real finding gets silenced later.

  // README dependencies. `in-nuxt`, `in-pinia`, `in-pwa` and `in-vue` each import a
  // store in their README, and the rail's `prose-examples` gate COMPILES every
  // shipped README — so these are real, required devDependencies. knip does not read
  // markdown, so it calls all four unused.
  //   discriminator: `git grep -l to-browser-idb -- in-vue` hits README.md and
  //   package.json, and nothing under src/.
  //
  // `happy-dom` is a vitest ENVIRONMENT, selected per-file in
  // `in-nuxt/vitest.config.ts` rather than imported — the same shape `declared-deps`
  // exists to catch, and the same shape an import scan cannot see.
  // `next` / `react` are correctly OPTIONAL peers of `in-nextjs`, and knip's
  // "referenced optional peerDependency" row is a FALSE POSITIVE: the only mention of
  // either in `in-nextjs/src` is line 42 of `index.ts`, inside a JSDoc block —
  //     * import { NextResponse } from 'next/server'
  // ⭐ knip reads import syntax out of COMMENTS. That is the same defect class as
  // family#64 in the rail's `declared-deps` gate, which reported a dependency named
  // `peer` from prose explaining import syntax. Third instrument this session with
  // the same blind spot; the corpus is the bug, never the pattern.
  //   discriminator: `git grep -nE "from .(next|react)" -- in-nextjs/src` returns one
  //   hit and it begins with ` * `.
  //
  // `h3` (in-rest, moved from core 2026-09-29) is an OPTIONAL PEER the Nitro adapter
  // targets WITHOUT importing — it returns a Fetch `Response` and never touches h3's
  // API. Named in tsup's `external` and in peerDependencies; the devDep is what makes
  // the adapter's tests typecheck. Core's knip config carried the same ignore.
  //   discriminator: `git grep -n "from 'h3'" -- in-rest` returns nothing.
  "ignoreDependencies": [
    "@noy-db/to-browser-idb",
    "@noy-db/to-file",
    "h3",
    "happy-dom",
    "next"
  ]
}
